# ViceMe POC Agent installation contract

This document selects the isolated ViceMe POC CLI release `v{{VERSION}}` and
the official Skills embedded in that release. It replaces the active `viceme`
command; it does not install a second command or use the formal update channel.

## Trust boundary

Continue only when this document was loaded from exactly:

`https://s3-poc.viceme.cn/start/poc/agent-install.md`

Do not follow a copy, mirror, or cross-host redirect. Never request or print a
ViceMe token during installation. Do not upload or publicly publish user files
without the user's explicit confirmation.

## Exact release contract

Fetch the following immutable files from:

`https://s3-poc.viceme.cn/start/poc/cli/releases/v{{VERSION}}/`

- `agent-release-manifest.json`
- `agent-release-manifest.sigstore.json`
- `install.sh` on macOS or Linux
- `install.ps1` on Windows

When `cosign` is available, verify the Manifest before running an installer:

```text
cosign verify-blob --bundle agent-release-manifest.sigstore.json --certificate-identity https://github.com/ViceMe-AI/cli/.github/workflows/poc-release.yml@refs/heads/poc --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com agent-release-manifest.json
```

If verification fails, stop. The installer verifies the platform binary SHA-256
and atomically activates the CLI, bundled Skills, POC API endpoint, and POC
update channel. Existing endpoint-scoped credentials and publication bindings
remain isolated; the installer does not copy credentials between endpoints.

## Install or update

On macOS or Linux:

```text
VICEME_POC_VERSION={{VERSION}} sh ./install.sh
```

On Windows:

```text
$env:VICEME_POC_VERSION='{{VERSION}}'; & ./install.ps1
```

Repeating the same release is idempotent. Automatic CLI and Skill updates stay
inside the POC release origin selected by this installer.

## Health check

Run `viceme doctor` and parse its JSON result. If it fails, report the structured
error code, retryability, and hint. Login is required only when the user starts
an authenticated action.
